   <text type="letter">
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline><date when="1942-03-18">March 18. 1942</date></dateline><lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4303" type="person">Dr. Horace Kallen</rs><lb/> New
               School of Social Research<lb/> 66 West 12 Str.<lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York City</rs>
               <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4303" type="person">Mr.
                  Kallen</rs>:</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>I have received the enclosed letter <note type="ea">liegt nicht vor</note> and I do
               not know what to answer. Have you any idea about a subject we could advise this man
               to deal with, a subject which, of course, would demand more thought than reading
               because he has no books in his camp. I would be very grateful in the interest of <rs
                  ref="#tillich_person_id__4304" type="person">Mr. Manfred Saalheimer</rs> for a
               suggestion coming from you.</p>
            <closer>
               <salute>Very sincerely yours</salute>
               <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person"
                  ><hi rend="hand">Paul Tillich</hi><lb/>Paul Tillich</rs></signed>
            </closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
